.TH "ZYPPER-DECLARATIVE" "1" "June 2026" "zypper-declarative 0.6.2" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
zypper-declarative - declarative reconciling converger surfaced as a
zypper subcommand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]zypper declarative\f[R] \f[I]verb\f[R] [\f[I]key=value\f[R] \&...]
.PP
\f[B]zypper-declarative\f[R] \f[I]verb\f[R] [\f[I]key=value\f[R] \&...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]zypper-declarative\f[R] converges a SUSE system to a desired
manifest inside a single snapshot transaction, recording what was
applied.
The manifest is the declarable subset of the SUSE Machinery system
description: \f[B]packages\f[R], \f[B]repositories\f[R],
\f[B]services\f[R], and \f[B]config_files\f[R].
Its canonical serialisation is JSON (Machinery \f[V]format_version\f[R]
1); YAML is an opt-in alternative serialisation of the identical data
model.
.PP
Options use \f[B]key=value\f[R] syntax (POSIX \f[V]--flag\f[R] style is
not used for options).
Bare-word global commands \f[B]version\f[R] and \f[B]help\f[R] are
accepted, with \f[V]--version\f[R], \f[V]--help\f[R], and \f[V]-h\f[R]
as tolerated aliases.
.SH VERBS
.TP
\f[B]apply\f[R]
Converge the system to the desired manifest inside a snapshot
transaction.
Idempotent.
.TP
\f[B]diff\f[R]
Dry run.
Print what \f[B]apply\f[R] would change, making no modification and
opening no transaction.
.TP
\f[B]verify\f[R]
Check whether the actual state equals a reference declaration, modulo
the keep-list.
.TP
\f[B]status\f[R]
Print the current declarative state: which manifest is applied, the
generation, and a one-line drift summary.
.TP
\f[B]describe\f[R]
Read the actual state of the declarable scopes and emit it in the
selected serialisation (JSON by default, YAML on request).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]mode=auto|external|internal\f[R]
Transaction binding.
Default \f[B]auto\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]manifest-path=\f[R]<path>
Desired manifest (apply, diff); reference manifest for verify.
.TP
\f[B]format=json|yaml\f[R]
Serialisation for this invocation\[cq]s manifest I/O.
When omitted, the operative file extension decides, else
\f[B]manifest-format\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]state-path=\f[R]<path>
Captured actual state for verify and diff (offline; default reads the
live system).
.TP
\f[B]root=\f[R]<path>
Root to describe.
Default \f[B]/\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]out=\f[R]<path>
describe output file.
Default stdout.
.TP
\f[B]on-unreadable=error|warn\f[R]
describe handling of an unreadable scope source.
Default \f[B]error\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]scope=etc|full\f[R]
describe/verify read scope.
\f[B]etc\f[R] (default) inspects only /etc; \f[B]full\f[R] also audits
/usr and /boot (expensive, opt-in).
.PP
Additional CONFIG knobs accepted as key=value options:
\f[B]manifest-format\f[R], \f[B]repo-lock\f[R], \f[B]content-store\f[R],
\f[B]keep-list\f[R], \f[B]signature-verification\f[R],
\f[B]keyring\f[R], \f[B]activation-policy\f[R], \f[B]applied-root\f[R].
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Success: convergence complete or no-op, system matches declaration, or
describe produced output.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
Logical failure: convergence failed and discarded; verify found drift;
manifest invalid, unsafe-YAML, or unverified; state collection failed.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
Invocation error: bad arguments; unknown format value; manifest
unreadable; insufficient privilege; transaction mechanism unavailable;
output path unwritable; malformed state dump.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[B]/usr/lib/zypper-declarative/applied.json\f[R]
The applied record of a generation (stored inside the snapshot).
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
zypper(8), snapper(8), transactional-update(8)
.SH AUTHORS
Matthias G. Eckermann.
